{% comment %}
  blocks/icon-with-text.liquid

  An icon beside a short line of text. Trust points, shipping promises, feature
  rows.

  The icon is decorative and `aria-hidden`: the text beside it is the content,
  and announcing "truck, free delivery over fifty pounds" helps nobody.

  ## The mark is the theme's shared one

  `snippets/icon-mark.liquid` resolves the Shape and the Ring — the same three
  groups the Feature icon, the Highlight tile, the Accordion row and the
  footer's Utility item all offer. It emits nothing until a merchant chooses
  something, so this block still draws what it always drew: a bare glyph beside
  the words, with no box behind it.

  The wrapper around the glyph is new and paints nothing. It exists because a
  ring has to be positioned against *something*, and an `<svg>` that is itself
  the flex item has nowhere to hang one. `inline-flex` with `flex: 0 0 auto` is
  what the glyph had from `.icon`, so the row and the column arrangements
  measure exactly as they did.

  ## The source is stated, not inferred

  `custom_icon` used to win simply by holding an upload, so a merchant who had
  tried one and moved on could not get back to the theme glyph without clearing
  the field. **Icon** now says which, and the upload keeps its own id so nothing
  saved is lost — an item with no source stored falls back to the old rule.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  capture icon_px
    render 'icon-size', size: s.icon_size, custom: s.icon_size_custom
  endcapture
  assign icon_size = icon_px | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the upload has two homes ----

    The shared panel calls its image `icon_image`, which every other block that
    offers the mark uses. This block called it `custom_icon`, and renaming a
    setting in Shopify does not carry the value across — the upload would simply
    be gone from every block already using one.

    So the new id is read first and the old one is the fallback, exactly the way
    the Highlight tile still reads its retired `icon_frame_*` keys. The old
    field stays in the schema, hidden behind the same source, so a merchant can
    see and clear what they uploaded rather than being left with a picture they
    cannot reach.
  endcomment
  assign icon_upload = s.icon_image | default: s.custom_icon

  comment
    The old order, reproduced for anything saved before the select existed: an
    upload won if there was one, otherwise the theme glyph.
  endcomment
  assign icon_source = s.icon_source
  if icon_source == blank
    if icon_upload != blank
      assign icon_source = 'image'
    else
      assign icon_source = 'icon'
    endif
  endif

  assign has_icon = false
  if icon_source == 'icon' and s.icon != blank and s.icon != 'none'
    assign has_icon = true
  elsif icon_source == 'image' and icon_upload != blank
    assign has_icon = true
  endif

  comment
    The space between the icon and the words. It was a fixed `--space-3` in the
    stylesheet, which is right for a stacked card and too wide for a row of
    short labels where the icon should sit close enough to read as belonging to
    the text beside it.

    `plus: 0` and not a blank test: an unset range is nil in Shopify and
    Undefined elsewhere, and only one of those is blank — the difference that
    emits `--icon-text-gap:px` and takes the whole style attribute down with it.
  endcomment
  assign gap = block.settings.gap | default: 12 | plus: 0
-%}

{%- capture icon_text_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: block.settings, declarations: true -%}
  --icon-text-gap: {{ gap }}px;
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  On the wrapper and not on the block, because `.icon-mark` is matched on the
  presence of each property name in the element's *own* `style` attribute — a
  value inherited from an ancestor is invisible to that test, which is exactly
  what keeps a mark that set nothing from being restyled.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture icon_mark_style -%}
  {%- render 'icon-mark', block: s, declarations: true -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="block-icon-text icon-mark-host block-icon-text--{{ block.settings.alignment }}"
  data-block-spacing
  style="{{ icon_text_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if has_icon -%}
    <span class="block-icon-text__mark icon-mark" style="{{ icon_mark_style | strip_newlines | strip }}">
      {% render 'icon-mark', block: s %}
      {%- if icon_source == 'image' -%}
        {% render 'image', image: icon_upload, alt: s.icon_image_alt, ratio: 'square', sizes: '48px', wrapper_class: 'block-icon-text__custom' %}
      {%- else -%}
        {% render 'icon', icon: s.icon, size: icon_size, class: 'block-icon-text__icon' %}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="block-icon-text__body">
    {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <p class="block-icon-text__heading">{{ block.settings.heading }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
      <div class="block-icon-text__text rte">{{ block.settings.text }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

